**Definition of Confidential Information (NDA 7)**  

Confidential Information **includes all non‑public business, financial, technical, legal, operational, strategic, regulatory, and commercial material disclosed in oral, written, visual, digital, machine‑readable, or any other form, whether or not expressly marked as confidential**.  

It **also includes**:

- the existence, scope, timing, and status of discussions;  
- Tata’s internal evaluation criteria;  
- draft issue lists;  
- contract positions and redlines;  
- governance and approval pathways;  
- risk assessment outputs;  
- source code excerpts;  
- designs;  
- product roadmaps;  
- data dictionaries;  
- issue trackers;  
- security findings;  
- incident response measures; and  
- any notes, analyses, summaries, extracts, compilations, or derivative materials related to the foregoing.  

*Source:* “Definition of Confidential Information – NDA‑Wellness – NDA” – **Legal AI - Test_NDA (1)_NDA 7_Redacted (1)**【1】.  

